Compile LaTeX with no local TeX
	:comment Problem: keep the local machine clean
	:comment Approach: run latexmk in Docker over SSH
	Set up once
		$ make install
		$ make setup-network (optional)
		$ make build-docker
	Run on a .tex file@$ luatex-pdf document.tex
	Choose where to compile
		:if Local Docker chosen (-L)?
			Use the local Docker
		:else
			:if Global IP equals home IP?
				Use the internal host
			:else
				Use the external host
			:comment -H HOST overrides the choice
	Copy the .tex, styles and figures@to a temporary work directory
	Compile with latexmk in Docker
		:if Document class needs another engine?
			Switch the engine
		:else
			Keep the chosen engine (-e)
	:if PDF produced?
		Copy the PDF next to the .tex
	:else
		Report the failure (--show-log)
	Remove the temporary work directory
	:while Watch mode (-w) and a file changed?
		Sync, compile and retrieve again
	:terminal PDF beside the source
